# Origin of the Ephyra Go backend (Gin).
#
# Nitro proxies /api to it — in development and in the built server alike — so
# the frontend is always same-origin with the API. The backend sets its session
# cookie with SameSite=Lax and has no CORS middleware, so a cross-origin
# frontend could not authenticate at all.
#
# NUXT_BACKEND_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8080

# Serve the whole API from an in-browser mock, with no backend running.
#
# Defaults to on for `npm run dev` and off for a production build, so plain
# `npm run dev` works with nothing else installed. Override either way:
#
#   NUXT_PUBLIC_API_MOCK=false npm run dev     # real backend during development
#   NUXT_PUBLIC_API_MOCK=true  npm run build   # demo a build with no backend
#
# The mock reproduces the real routes, bodies, status codes and visibility rules
# (see app/mock/), and seeds a demo world: six accounts, five contests covering
# every phase, judge pools and nodes, and a rejudge flow. Every seeded account's
# password is `password123`; `alice@example.com` is a site admin.
#
# Toggle it at runtime from the mock console in the app header instead of
# restarting the dev server.
#
# NUXT_PUBLIC_API_MOCK=

# Base URL of the API as the browser sees it.
#
# Leave this unset: every request is same-origin and goes through the Nitro /api
# proxy. Set it only when the frontend is served from the backend's own origin
# directly, with no proxy in between.
#
# NUXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=
